WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.930
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I want to talk about everyone's

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.980
favourite super-baby, Jack-Jack, and explain
and rank his seventeen powers.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.070
If you're new here, I do regular Pixar and
superhero videos plus giveaways.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.070
To enter my latest giveaway, make sure you're
a subscriber, watch my video and let me know

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.820
your top three Jack-Jack powers.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.320
Spoilers ahead for Jack-Jack's scenes, so
take care if you haven't seen Incredibles

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.320
2 yet and remember you can add this video
to your watch-later playlist.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:39.080
We see this very briefly in Incredibles 2
when Jack-Jack sneezes.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.630
After Mr Incredible discovers Jack-Jack's
powers for the first time, we see a brief

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:48.380
lightning effect around the super-powered
baby suggesting he can summon electricity.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:52.640
In fact, it reminds me a bit of Thor's lightning
powers in the MCU.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.250
After Syndrome kidnapped Jack-Jack in the
first movie, the baby transformed into metal,

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.110
dragging the villain down and throwing him
off balance.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:05.360
Jack-Jack's levitation powers are a fun spectacle
we've seen in the short Jack-Jack Attack and

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.890
Incredibles 2, and it's something he appears
to be able to control quite well.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:13.509
Associated with this power is his ability
to reverse gravity selectively.

00:01:13.509 --> 00:01:18.340
For example, in the short, while Jack-Jack
hangs upside down on the ceiling, he maintains

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.450
his position but allows the milk from his
bottle to fall onto Kari.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.149
When manifesting his powers, Jack-Jack displays
various degrees of super-strength, durability

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:28.869
and resistance.

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:33.079
During the racoon fight, he physically wrestles,
kicks, and smacks the creature across the

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:36.530
yard, and he also picks up and throws garden
furniture with ease.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.360
In Jack-Jack Attack, he was able to chew his
way through a wooden playpen.

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.979
There wasn't any sign of wood left over either,
suggesting Jack-Jack's body can even cope

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:47.749
with digesting organic matter like wood.

00:01:47.749 --> 00:01:52.229
His skin is also pretty damage-resistant because
he can withstand fighting with the racoon

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:55.020
and even turning himself on fire.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:02:00.100
And that ability to burst into flames is pretty
cool and what he touches can catch fire too.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.840
He used this power against Syndrome in the
first movie, but it's something that often

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.950
seems to be triggered by emotion.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.710
It'd definitely be good to see him learn to
harness the ability more and even potentially

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.880
throw fireballs.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.840
Another cool power Jack-Jack has in Incredibles
2 is the ability to rocket jump or blast off

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.580
and that often seems to be brought on by a
sneeze.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:25.489
Jack-Jack has a sort of elasticity, similar
to his mother, where he can stretch his body,

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:28.080
for example, when he's attacked by the raccoon.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.140
And this could well be an important part of
his seeming invulnerability.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:36.220
There's an interesting moment in the Incredibile
when, after escaping from the hynoptised Supers

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:41.030
at the house, the Parr children are feeling
unsure about how to go forward.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:46.030
Jack-Jack levitates, rotates and at the same
time performs a weird reality distortion effect

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.120
that warps and wobbles the space inside the
car.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.049
This reminds the kids that they have a secret
weapon: their highly super-powered baby brother

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:56.459
and that kick-starts them into action.

00:02:56.459 --> 00:03:00.329
Seeing Jack-Jack create multiple copies of
himself is pretty awesome.

00:03:00.329 --> 00:03:04.980
This is a useful skill against an opponent,
and we see this when Jack-Jack attacks the

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.390
racoon, and it reminds me somewhat of Agent
Smith from The Matrix.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:13.579
Jack-Jack also self-multiplies at Edna's house
and while he's there we also get to see his

00:03:13.579 --> 00:03:15.150
power of mimicry.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:19.879
He can not only make himself look like the
feisty fashion designer, but he can also imitate

00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:22.250
her physical expressions.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:26.519
Jack-Jack used his ability to shapeshift into
a demon to ferociously good effect against

00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:27.519
Syndrome.

00:03:27.519 --> 00:03:32.200
As the infant transforms he gets red skin,
longer nails and sharper teeth, plus his muscles

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.380
expand giving him increased strength and manoeuvrability
which he uses to pull out Syndrome's hair

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.519
and attack his rocket boots.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:44.180
The sequel also shows Jack-Jack transforming
into a demon on multiple occasions and suggests

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:48.290
this power is often triggered when the toddler
gets angry, for example, when he's denied

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.829
a cookie.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:54.810
It's a pretty funny moment in Incredibles
2 when Jack-Jack grows into a giant baby,

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.870
bursting out of an air vent where he and his
siblings are hiding.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.620
He also then smashes and runs through a series
of metal walls in a moment that reminded me

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.319
of Juggernaut in X-Men 3.

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:08.829
Of course, with Ant-Man And The Wasp out this
year as well, I couldn't help but also think

00:04:08.829 --> 00:04:10.709
of Giant-Man.

00:04:10.709 --> 00:04:15.180
Jack-Jack's ability to teleport is an incredibly
useful one that first manifested in Jack-Jack

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:16.180
Attack.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:20.470
This is the first power he ever displayed
and happened just after Kari put on some classical

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:22.070
music by Mozart.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.229
The Parr family had always assumed Jack-Jack
was normal.

00:04:25.229 --> 00:04:30.380
But just after Kari puts on some Mozart, Jack-Jack
seems to perk up and his eyes dilate and in

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.539
the next few seconds his powers kick into
action.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:38.500
It seems it was Mozart that unlocked Jack-Jack's
latent superpowers because, as Kari says to

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.270
Helen,
"I also brought Mozart to play while he sleeps

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:44.319
because leading experts say Mozart makes babies
smarter."

00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:48.789
Phasing through solid objects like walls and
windows is another incredibly useful skill

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:52.650
as it means Jack-Jack isn't really constrained
by any physical boundaries.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:57.410
Kari witnessed this to hilarious effect in
Jack-Jack Attack and we also see him use it

00:04:57.410 --> 00:04:58.580
in Incredibles 2.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:04.710
Not only can Jack-Jack teleport between physical
locations, but he can also travel to other

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:08.479
dimensions and once there he can still even
communicate with our own dimension.

00:05:08.479 --> 00:05:09.479
"Cookie!

00:05:09.479 --> 00:05:11.250
Cha cha want a cookie?!"

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.630
"Nam nam cookie!"

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.940
"Cha cha want num num?"

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:19.570
By the way, the other dimension scene is a
fantastic easter egg to the classic horror

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:23.220
movie Poltergeist which I talk more about
in my easter eggs video.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:27.130
There's a link for that at the end of this
video and in the video description.

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:31.121
We first get a taste of Jack-Jack's telekinetic
powers when, during the raccoon scene, he

00:05:31.121 --> 00:05:34.400
uses his mind to raise the trash can lid off
the floor.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.720
And it's Jack-Jack who ultimately breaks the
hypnotic spell cast on Elastigirl when he

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.580
telekinetically removes her googles.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.620
Jack-Jack's telekinesis is a new ability that
we see for the first time in the sequel and

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:49.660
this power's been wielded by some of the most
powerful heroes on screen.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:54.860
Think Professor X and Jean Grey from the X-Men
and Eleven from Stranger Things.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:59.380
Jack-Jack's seventeen powers are all fantastic,
so deciding on my favourite was tough, but

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:03.229
his laser vision and how he uses it in the
raccoon scene is pretty amazing.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:07.910
We did see the laser eyes for the first time
in Jack-Jack Attack where Kari used a hand-mirror

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:12.639
to deflect the rays, however, one of the funniest
moments in Incredibles 2 has to be when Bob

00:06:12.639 --> 00:06:18.600
turns Jack-Jack into a kind of baby laser
gun.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:25.169
Now, what your three favourite Jack-Jack powers?

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:28.139
And what would you like to see him do if there's
another sequel?

